      "content": "An escrow agent is a neutral third party in a real estate transaction who holds funds and documents on behalf of both the buyer and seller to ensure the deal proceeds fairly. They are required to hold your money until specific conditions like a clear title, passed inspections, and signed contracts are met before disbursing payments or transferring the deed. This process protects you both by preventing situations where you exchange funds without the other party fulfilling their obligations, effectively reducing the risk of fraud or legal disputes. While it may feel strange to have your money tied up for weeks, it is a standard safety net that facilitates trust in high-value transactions like buying a home in Seattle.",
